<title>TURKEY: Turkish Migros Q1 net rises 55 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Migros Q1 net rises 55 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   428.29   vs   724.12</p>
<p>    Net profit		    404.73   vs   260.68</p>
<p>    Net sales		  18,131.68   vs 8,101.01</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    114.32   vs   117.57</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  535.64   vs   276.00</p>
<p>    Interest paid		     0    vs	  0</p>
<p>    Total debts		12,061.24   vs  5,703.40</p>
<p>    Equity			3,807.83   vs  1,784.35</p>
<p>    Capital			 945.00   vs    360.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading supermarket chain Migros Turk T.A.S. is owned 55.11 percent by Temel Ticaret, an affiliate of leading industrial Koc conglomerate.</p>
<p>The company will pay a 500 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from 1996 profits from May 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
